# Scenario: clinician and patient discuss two-sided considerations for anticoagulation.
comparison "Start direct oral anticoagulation?"
mode: pros-cons
pro "Reduces stroke risk in atrial fibrillation"
pro "No routine INR monitoring"
pro "Fixed daily dosing"
con "Bleeding risk requires counselling"
con "Cost may exceed warfarin"
con "Renal function needs periodic review"
